  "oxlintComments": {
    "core: no-use-before-define": "`variables: false` skips a reference from inside a function to a variable declared later in an outer scope, which can't run before the declaration does unless the function is called during load. Functions that call each other have no order that satisfies the default. A use in the same scope, and a function or class used before it, still report. https://www.ultracite.ai/research/func-style",
    "core: unicorn/no-nested-ternary": "Its fixer wraps the inner ternary in parentheses that oxfmt strips, so every `fix` run ping-pongs. eslint-config-prettier disables it for the same reason; the core `no-nested-ternary` still reports the construct.",
    "core: unicorn/no-useless-undefined": "A required parameter typed `T | undefined` has to be passed `undefined` explicitly, and the rule's autofix deletes it into a TS2554 error (#851). The rule can't see parameter types, so skip call arguments. Not a TypeScript-only override: oxlint applies a preset's overrides after the user's own `rules`, so it would undo their settings.",
    "js-plugins: sonarjs/cognitive-complexity": "The same number as Biome's noExcessiveCognitiveComplexity limit, but the two score functions differently, so the limits aren't equivalent."
  },
